2. FIRST UNDERSTAND THE BIG PICTURE

Before writing JavaScript code, understand where JavaScript fits.
A website can be thought of as having three major responsibilities:
HTML → STRUCTURE
HTML answers:
"What is present on the webpage?"
Example:
<h1>Welcome</h1>
<button>Login</button>
<p>Hello</p>
HTML creates the elements.

CSS → APPEARANCE
CSS answers:
"How should those elements look?"
Example:
button {
    background: blue;
    color: white;
}
CSS controls appearance and presentation.


JavaScript → BEHAVIOUR
JavaScript answers:
"What should happen?"
For example:
What happens when I click a button?
What happens when I type into a form?
What happens when I submit a form?
How should the page react?
How can I get data from a server?
How can I change something on the page?

Example:
console.log("Button clicked");
Later:
button.addEventListener("click", login);

