6. What is ES6?
ES6 is an important version of ECMAScript.
It was officially released in 2015.
Therefore, ES6 is also called:
ECMAScript 2015
ES6 introduced many important features to JavaScript.
For example:
let name = "John";
const age = 20;
The let and const keywords were introduced with ES6.
We will learn these features in detail later.

7. Why Should a JavaScript Developer Know ECMAScript?
