11. WHAT IS A JAVASCRIPT ENGINE?
A JavaScript engine is software that reads and executes JavaScript code.
Different browsers use different engines.
Important engines
Engine	Used by
V8	Chrome, Edge, Node.js
SpiderMonkey	Firefox
JavaScriptCore	Safari
The uploaded material specifically identifies these three engines and their environments.

12. WHAT HAPPENS BEFORE JAVASCRIPT EXECUTES?
At a simplified level:
Step 1 — Browser receives the page
HTML downloaded
Step 2 — Browser encounters JavaScript
For example:
<script src="app.js"></script>
Step 3 — JavaScript engine receives the code
Step 4 — Engine parses the code
It checks whether the code follows valid syntax.
Step 5 — Engine executes the code
The statements execute in execution order.

13. PARSE VS EXECUTE
These two words are important for interviews.
Parse => understand the code
The engine examines(read) the code and understands its structure.
Example:
console.log("Hello");

Execute => execute the code
The engine actually performs the instruction.
console.log("Hello");
causes:
Hello
to appear in the console.

14. IMPORTANT EXECUTION RULE
For the beginner model:
JavaScript statements execute in order, from top to bottom.
Example:
console.log("second");
console.log("third");
console.log("first");

Output:
Second
third
first
Therefore, when solving output questions:
ALWAYS TRACE IN EXECUTION ORDER.





15. SYNTAX ERROR VS RUNTIME ERROR
This distinction is extremely important for interviews.

What is syntax?
Syntax = rules for writing JavaScript code correctly.

What  is Syntax Error ?
A syntax error means the code is written in a way that JavaScript cannot properly understand.
Example:
console.log("Hello);
The string is not properly closed.
The engine cannot correctly parse(understand) the code.

Runtime Error
The code starts executing, but an error occurs while it is running.
Example:
console.log("Start");

console.log(Hello);

console.log("End");
If Hello has not been declared, execution reaches that line and fails.
Therefore:
Start
ReferenceError
End does not execute.

16. EASY WAY TO REMEMBER THE DIFFERENCE
Syntax Error
Can the engine understand the code?
             ↓
          NO
             ↓
       Syntax Error
Runtime Error
Code can be understood
          ↓
Code starts running
          ↓
Problem occurs during execution
          ↓
Runtime Error




Syntax Error	Runtime Error
Problem with code structure	Problem while running
JavaScript cannot properly understand the code	JavaScript starts running but encounters a problem
Happens during code parsing	Happens during execution

Syntax Error
    ↓
"Your sentence is written incorrectly."

Runtime Error
    ↓
"Your sentence is understandable,
but something goes wrong when you try to perform it."

