JavaScript has Automatic Semicolon Insertion (ASI).
Therefore semicolons are technically not required in every situation.
But for this course:
End statements with semicolons consistently.
Interview answer
Semicolons are technically optional because JavaScript has Automatic Semicolon Insertion, but using them consistently improves readability and avoids certain edge cases.

